From 0c57293711f6fd7cd56be001bc2ee1d9b2e11410 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 02:15:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): kanban_create refuses a second owner of one
 red-CI failure (same failing test or Actions run) [daveey]

Five cards owned test_busy_board_open_does_not_block_session_poll on 11-02 (run 41516070553) and two owned the
termux assembly failure on 11-03: their titles share too few words for the word-overlap rule. A card now names
failing tests (title test_ names, node ids in a failing sentence of the opening paragraph, FAILED log lines) and
Actions runs; an open card naming the same test function, or the same run when neither names a test, refuses the
create (create_overlap) unless lineage, waits-on, recovers, a citation of the owner's id, or distinct_from applies.
t_01a19ea9f1739df6
