+  "body": "Main CI run https://github.com/daveey/hermes/actions/runs/41556904515 (head c34694e325d), job \"Python tests / Termux assembly permissions\" (125665322801) failed:\n\n```\nFAILED tests/scripts/test_termux_assembly_permissions.py::test_assembly_publishes_facts_as_termux_uid_and_returns_host_owned_output[success] - FileExistsError: [Errno 17] File exists: '/opt/actions-runner/_work/_temp/termux-assembly/test_assembly_publishes_facts_0/payload'\n(same for [failed-build], ..._1/payload)\n```\n\nCause (from the code at tests/scripts/test_termux_assembly_permissions.py:51): with `HERMES_TEST_DOCKER_MOUNT_ROOT` set, the payload dir is `mount_root / tmp_path.name / \"payload\"`. `tmp_path.name` (`test_assembly_publishes_facts_0`) is only unique within one pytest basetemp, but the mount root is a runner-temp dir shared across runs on the long-lived docker-ci runner, so a leftover from a previous run collides and `mkdir(parents=True)` raises.\n\nFix: make the per-test dir unique and owned by the test (e.g. `tempfile.mkdtemp(dir=mount_root)` or include a uuid/pid), and clean it up in a finalizer (contents may be owned by the container uid: use the same container to chown/rm, or rm with tolerant handling). Do not just add exist_ok=True (stale content from another run would leak into the assertions).\n\nDone when: the PR is merged to main and the Termux assembly permissions job is green on main's next CI run. Prior related deflake cards: t_01a1899a15eff3c8, t_01a187714d4b30a9 (done).",
