+  "body": "Found while getting main CI green (t_7131b872, PR https://github.com/daveey/hermes/pull/32).\n\nThe test fails intermittently on the self-hosted hermes-hub runners:\n- FAILED on main push run https://github.com/daveey/hermes/actions/runs/39886244584 (job 120195193519, \"Python tests / Run tests (1/2)\"): `assert [] == [('Checking the docs first.', False)]` at tests/gateway/test_session_api.py:1377. The session SSE stream had no `assistant.commentary` event; `assistant.completed` was present.\n- PASSED in PR #30 run 39886091334 on the same code (except #30's one-line workflow change).\n\nWhat we know: `_commentary` (gateway/platforms/api_server.py ~3657) calls `events.enqueue`, and `_SessionEventQueue.enqueue` hops to the loop with `call_soon_threadsafe` when it runs off-loop. The fake agent calls `interim(...)` inside `run_conversation`. Find out why the event goes missing under load. It might be an ordering race between the enqueue hop and `run_agent`'s completion, something leaking from an earlier test in the file (gateway config / display.interim_assistant_messages cache), or an executor/loop mismatch. If it's a real product race, so commentary can be lost or reordered after `assistant.completed`, fix the product code, not the test.\n\nRepro: run the file on hermes-hub (`ssh -i ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 -o IdentitiesOnly=yes ubuntu@192.0.2.10`), under load and in a loop, with scripts/run_tests.sh. Fork commits are tagged `[daveey]`. Merge once the PR's CI is green. Done when there's a root cause, a fix merged, and 20+ loop runs green.",
